SUMMARY:Survivalist Series: Introduction to Firecraft
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our websi
 te.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/fire-craft-intro-4)**\n***
 Discover the ancient art of safely creating and maintaining fire without l
 ighters or matches!***\nFor thousands of years\, fire has been our greates
 t ally for warmth\, safety\, cooking\, and survival. But in the wild\, fir
 e doesn’t come easy. It takes knowledge\, patience\, and the right techn
 ique.\nWe are back for the fourth installment of this popular course to te
 ach you the beautiful art of fire. You’ll begin to master the craft with
  hands-on guidance from our expert firecraft instructor - guide Kyle.\nYou
 'll be shown and encouraged to practice:\n1\\. Ferrocerium rod techniques 
 with multiple tinders\n2\\. Traditional flint & steel fire lighting\n3\\. 
 The art of hand\\-drill friction fire\nThis course will give you the found
 ation to create fire anywhere\, anytime.\n**Included:** Your own high-qual
 ity ferro rod to take home and keep the fire burning wherever you go.\n**W
 ho It’s For:** This course is for beginners and intermediate survivalist
 s alike. Bring your curiosity\, a willingness to learn\, and a love of get
 ting outside. This is an amazing opportunity not only to learn from our ex
 pert\, but it's a fun\, practical lesson at a uniquely low price.\n**About
  this series:** The Survivalist Series is an expert-led set of courses des
 igned to develop applicable and life-saving skills in the outdoors. Keep y
 our eyes peeled for more courses on many other topics coming soon!\n**Due 
 to the cost of parking at Bronte Creek\, WU transport is recommended for t
 his course.**\n**Accessibility**\nWilderness Union is committed to making 
 our adventures as accessible as possible. If you wish to make an accommoda
 tion request relating to a disability or provide feedback\, please do so b
 y sending an email to info@wildernessunion.com\n**Highlights**\n**Ancient 
 techniques:** Learn unique firecraft techniques from long ago that do not 
 need matches or a lighter.\n**Survivalist skills training:** Develop essen
 tial skills to survive and thrive in the wild.\n**Fire kit included:** Eve
 ry participant gets this kit including a ferro rod and variety of tinders.
 \n**Itinerary**\n**10:00** \\- Shuttle leaves from near Keele station\n**1
 1:00** \\- Arrive at course location\n**11:00 - 16:00** \\- Introduction t
 o fire craft course\n**16:00 - 17:00** \\- Drive back to Toronto\n**Event 
 cost: $104+HST. $20 optional transport also available. Please register [he
 re.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/fire-craft-intro-4)**\n**A
 bout Wilderness Union**\nWilderness Union is deliberate about building an 
 outdoors community that connects you to the life-changing magic of the out
 doors and helps you find your people.\nMembers range from 20-40 years old.
  The group is a mix of GTA locals and newcomers to Toronto from within Can
 ada and abroad.\nAttendance numbers on Meetup don't reflect our actual eve
 nt attendance - we typically have 15-20 community members at each event. L
 arge enough that there's someone new to meet but small enough that it's no
 t overwhelming!\n***Learn more at our website [www.wildernessunion.com](ht
 tps://www.wildernessunion.com/)***
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/wildernessunion/events/316861725/
